  "provenance_caveat": "All counts here are the SAME already-committed, already-verified raw counts from stephenson_sample_subtype_cell_counts_v1.tsv (source: the per-cohort RAW, provisional stephenson_monocyte_raw.h5ad) -- no new h5ad read was performed to build this table. The per-subtype cutoff sensitivity numbers are a DESCRIPTIVE exploration of how many donors would qualify at illustrative thresholds, NOT a new inclusion/QC rule, NOT a subtype choice, and NOT a claim that the surviving donors are ready for a real DE run.",
  "qc_admitted_input_status": "NOT FOUND. This round searched the repository for a QC-admitted (post-retention, not merely raw) monocyte analysis input -- a retention manifest or a QC'd object joinable to these annotations by sample/cell identity -- and found none. `stephenson_monocyte_raw.h5ad` (the only per-cohort object carrying `orig_celltype`) is explicitly `provisional` (MONOCYTE_PILOT_PREREG_v1.md Sec.3), the same status as `monocyte_pilot_feasibility_v3.tsv`'s Stephenson row. docs/current-status.md line 732 states the broader platelet-level QC rebuild is unfinished, so historical downstream numbers (which would include any monocyte retention decision) remain provisional. No monocyte-specific retention/QC-admission artifact exists anywhere under scripts/34_scfm_discovery_framework/ or scripts/32_rebuild_upfront_qc/ as of this check. The counts in this table are real, confirmed counts WITHIN the raw provisional object -- never read as 'final QC-admitted cell counts for an analysis'.",
